// Each entry is a FALSE POSITIVE arising because cppcheck assumes hosted C
// semantics. Bare-metal code legitimately violates those assumptions.
// Nothing here hides a real defect. Rationale per entry:
//
// comparePointers  - _sdata/_edata are LINKER-defined bounds of one region;
//                    in C they look like unrelated externs. Standard idiom.
// duplicateExpression - s_ticks is volatile and incremented by the SysTick
//                    ISR between the two reads; the substitution cppcheck
//                    performs is invalid. Unsigned subtraction is deliberate
//                    so the comparison survives the 49-day wrap.
// unusedStructMember - peripheral structs must declare every register and
//                    reserved gap or the member offsets stop matching silicon.
// constParameter*  - advisory; const on a pointer-to-volatile-peripheral adds
//                    nothing and breaks API consistency across the drivers.
comparePointers:src/startup_stm32f103rb.c
duplicateExpression:src/systick.c
unusedStructMember
constParameterPointer
